## # uv
##
## High-performance OS kernel I/O multiplexing engine.
## Part of the Alya Language package ecosystem (https://github.com/alya-lang).
##
## Wraps `WSAPoll`/`epoll`/`kqueue` readiness polling plus a Windows IOCP
## style async completion queue behind poller factories.

import "./types.alya"
import "./ffi.alya"
import "./core/poller.alya"

## Convenience factory creating an initialized `UvPoller`.
##
## ### Parameters
## - `initial_capacity`: Pre-sized descriptor slots. Defaults to `64`.
## - `max_events_batch`: Maximum events per wait batch. Defaults to `64`.
##
## ### Returns
## The new `UvPoller` instance (null when native creation fails).
##
## ### Examples
## ```alya
## let p = poller(32, 32)
## ```
pub function poller(initial_capacity = 64, max_events_batch = 64)
    return poller_new(initial_capacity, max_events_batch)
end

## Returns the active OS kernel multiplexer name.
##
## One of `"WSAPoll"`, `"epoll"`, `"kqueue"`, or `"poll"`.
##
## ### Returns
## The backend name string.
pub function backend_name() -> string
    return alya_uv_backend_name()
end

## Convenience factory creating an async completion queue.
##
## ### Parameters
## - `max_threads`: Worker thread hint (`0` selects a default). Defaults to `0`.
##
## ### Returns
## The new `UvIocp` instance (null when native creation fails).
pub function iocp(max_threads = 0)
    return iocp_new(max_threads)
end
